{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "SASH WINDOW REPLACEMENT (COMPLIANCE): Notwithstanding the drawings hereby approved all new sash windows shall accurately replicate, in terms of material, profile and detailing, the original windows surviving to the property.  They shall be painted timber, double hung traditional sliding sashes with weights and pullies to match the original style with narrow integral (not applied) glazing bars with a putty finish (not timber bead).  The glazing shall be no greater than 12mm (4mm glass : 4mm gas : 4mm glass) in total thickness. No horns, trickle vents or metallic/perforated spacer bars are permitted.  \r\n \r\nREASON: In order to preserve the special architectural or historic interest of the heritage asset"
  ],
